{
 "manufacturer": "Wilo",
 "manufacturer_slug": "wilo",
 "model": "Yonos GIGA2.0 with CIF module Modbus RTU",
 "model_slug": "yonos-giga2-0-cif-modbus",
 "short_model": "Yonos GIGA2.0",
 "aliases": [
  "Yonos GIGA2.0-I",
  "Yonos GIGA2.0-D",
  "Wilo-Yonos GIGA2.0"
 ],
 "equipment_type": "Pump (high-efficiency inline circulator)",
 "applies_to": "Wilo Yonos GIGA2.0 pumps fitted with the plug-in CIF module Modbus RTU (module firmware 1.00-99.99); registers needing a newer module are marked.",
 "summary": "The Wilo Yonos GIGA2.0 gets Modbus RTU through Wilo's plug-in CIF module. A master switches the pump on/off with the pump command word, selects the control mode and writes a relative duty point in 0.5 % steps; a bus command timer can fall back to preset values when communication stops. Read-only data covers head, flow, power, energy, speed, temperatures and status/error words. This map keeps only the points Wilo marks as supported on the Yonos GIGA2.0.",
 "transport": [
  "RTU"
 ],
 "defaults": {
  "unit_id": null,
  "baud": null,
  "parity": null,
  "data_bits": 8,
  "stop_bits": null,
  "tcp_port": null
 },
 "addressing": {
  "convention": "0-based",
  "note": "Wilo states that all register addresses are raw addresses as sent on the bus; its example frame 01 04 02 BC 00 01 reads input register 700 (0x02BC). Masters that count registers from 1 must add 1."
 },
 "default_word_order": "ABCD",
 "firmware": "CIF module Modbus RTU 1.00-99.99 (module versions per register as noted)",
 "source": {
  "title": "WILO Modbus RTU",
  "doc_number": "wilo194406",
  "revision_date": null,
  "url": "https://cms.media.wilo.com/cdndoc/wilo194406/11516106/wilo194406.html",
  "pages": "HTML sections 6.1.4 (data types and 32-bit order), 6.1.5 (error values), 6.2.6 (raw addressing note), 6.2.7.3 (holding registers), 6.2.7.4 (input registers), 8.2.3-8.2.4 (baud and frame codes), 8.3 (example frame)"
 },
 "notes": [
  "Source is Wilo's public HTML functional description for the CIF module Modbus RTU, which marks every register and every enumeration/bit value with the pump families that support it. Only registers, values and bits marked for Yonos GIGA2.0 are kept here; values and bits not listed are not supported on this pump. Facts are re-keyed and the document is linked, not re-hosted.",
  "32-bit values (REAL = FLOAT32, UDINT = UINT32) are stored with the most significant 16 bits at the base address (ABCD), as stated in section 6.1.4.",
  "Scale: engineering value = raw x scale from Wilo's list (e.g. pressure x 10 = cm H2O, operation time x 10 = h, flow x 0.1 = m3/h, duty point x 0.5 = %, temperatures x 0.1 = K).",
  "Temperatures are in kelvin with scale 0.1 (raw 2932 = 293.2 K, about 20 °C).",
  "Error values: an unavailable reading returns the largest positive value of its data type (65535 for UINT, 32767 for INT).",
  "Flow (input register 2): Wilo lists it twice with the same address, type and scale; up to module 6.00 its error value is 9999, from 6.01 it is 65535.",
  "Module-version requirements from the list are noted in descriptions ('Module 3.01+' etc.); registers without a note exist from module version 1.00.",
  "Left out: identification registers (700-750: BCD software revisions, vendor ID, UUID, article number), system time (502), energy-meter start timestamps (306/310), the double-pump total runtime (9) and 'pressure max-pres-value' (212, ambiguous between live and maximum pressure)."
 ],
